{
  "id": "waterfront",
  "name": "The Waterfront Quay",
  "notes": [
    "COMPOSITION. One long diagonal shoreline runs from the upper right down to",
    "the lower left, so the frame splits into a working stone quay (right, two",
    "thirds) and the harbour basin (left, one third) with the ships in it. The",
    "junk is the focal mass: 230px of hull with her rig breaking the top of the",
    "frame, moored where the diagonal meets the top edge, exactly on the third.",
    "",
    "WATER is ~34% of the frame before the hulls and the pier cover part of it.",
    "It is painted by the `water-field` prop rather than by a ground material:",
    "the layout declares a water `backdrop` (which is what makes the walk mask",
    "blocked out there), the ground regions carve the land out of it, and the",
    "prop repaints every remaining backdrop pixel in screen space with the",
    "sky-reflection ramp, wave banding and the glitter path. See texture.cjs.",
    "",
    "DEPTH PLANES. 1) headland + far roofline + distant sails, hazed hard.",
    "2) the basin, the ships, the pier, the quay and its godowns. 3) the near",
    "cargo rows and the bottom-left godown, which is emitted as a walk-behind",
    "overlay so the player can pass in front of and behind it.",
    "",
    "CULTURE MARKERS: the Fujian junk with her oculus and stern name-board, the",
    "guild signboard, the Gujarati dhow's lateen rig, the Portuguese padrao and",
    "the customs house flying the Cross of Christ."
  ],
